1
00:00:01,990 --> 00:00:05,470
الحمد لله و الصلاة و السلام على رسول الله و على آله و صحبه أجمعين

2
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:07,530
السلام عليكم و رحمة الله تعلى و بركاته

3
00:00:08,029 --> 00:00:12,000
So we are now moving into the second section of the study

4
00:00:12,030 --> 00:00:14,860
and that is coherence within passages of the Qur'ān.

5
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:18,170
And I use the word passage, sort of an invention of my own.

6
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:21,590
The Qur'ān clearly does not have paragraphs or indents

7
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:24,040
where you can tell one paragraph ended and

8
00:00:24,030 --> 00:00:25,980
the next one began and the next one began it's not like that.

9
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:27,860
It's just all the Ayāt are bunched together

10
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:30,550
in one sūrāh. The only distinguishable

11
00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:34,210
units of the Qur'ān are sūrah and āyah, right?

12
00:00:34,210 --> 00:00:36,760
Those are the only units of the Qur'ān that we know about.

13
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:39,250
Regardless of that,

14
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:43,640
what I want you to know is, Inshāllāh after this this discussion,

15
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,000
when we get into the structure of sūrahs themselves,

16
00:00:46,010 --> 00:00:48,940
then I'll say some things about the word sūrah and

17
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:51,310
the word āyah and how they correspond with each other.

18
00:00:51,310 --> 00:00:54,630
It'll be the next unit, but before we get there, right now

19
00:00:54,630 --> 00:00:56,250
I want to define what "passage" means.

20
00:00:56,440 --> 00:00:59,310
It's very distinct that sometimes there's a group of

21
00:00:59,310 --> 00:01:01,560
āyāt that are dealing with a similar subject.

22
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:05,260
Okay, you can tell. Okay, these are āyāt about Musa and Fir'own.

23
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:08,930
And then the subject is going to switch to the Ahkirah or something like that,

24
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:12,530
or these āyāt are about different things Allāh created.

25
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:15,360
And then there's gonna be a set of āyāt about the afterlife.

26
00:01:15,370 --> 00:01:18,360
You could clearly tell there's a change of subject and

27
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:21,840
the next group of āyāt are one distinct topic,

28
00:01:21,850 --> 00:01:24,737
right? Or for example, when you have وَٱلْعَـٰدِيَـٰتِ ضَبْحًۭا

29
00:01:24,762 --> 00:01:25,822
فَٱلْمُورِيَـٰتِ قَدْحًۭا

30
00:01:25,847 --> 00:01:27,224
فَٱلْمُغِيرَٰتِ صُبْحًۭا

31
00:01:27,234 --> 00:01:28,160
فَأَثَرْنَ بِهِۦ نَقْعًۭا

32
00:01:28,234 --> 00:01:29,680
فَوَسَطْنَ بِهِۦ جَمْعًا

33
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:35,010
Those are one distinct subject. (فَا، فَا، فَا، فَا). This then this, then this, then this, then this.

34
00:01:35,020 --> 00:01:37,770
They're one distinct subject. That's what I'm calling a 'passage'.

35
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:39,530
You can use different words for it.

36
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:43,150
Orientalists, and other Western academics use words like 'section'.

37
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:46,360
They say section one, section two, section three and then subsection.

38
00:01:46,370 --> 00:01:47,880
I've used that in the past also.

39
00:01:47,950 --> 00:01:51,150
But for the purposes of ease, I'm just calling them 'passages'. Now

40
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:55,220
there are two kinds of studies we're going to do when we study the nazm (Coherence)

41
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:57,760
the structure and the organization of passages.

42
00:01:57,770 --> 00:02:00,190
We're talking about a distinct set of āyāt.

43
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:03,200
Basically, what I'm saying is more than an āyah, but less than a sūrah.

44
00:02:03,210 --> 00:02:04,850
That's what we're talking about right now. Okay?

45
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:08,690
And when we do that, there's two ways of studying it.

46
00:02:08,699 --> 00:02:11,360
One is, how is an argument progressing?

47
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:16,900
How is it going from--How is the point being made from, the first of these āyat

48
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:19,010
to the second to the third to the fourth to the fifth?

49
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:22,510
And is it leading to a conclusion? Are they escalating in something?

50
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:24,580
Are they reaching a conclusion towards something?

51
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:28,060
Are they building upon an idea that was previously built or stated?

52
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:31,190
Some of that you already saw when we were discussing

53
00:02:31,190 --> 00:02:33,940
āyāt that were unrelated or looked unrelated.

54
00:02:33,950 --> 00:02:36,660
When I was translating the passage that led up to them,

55
00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:39,320
you could see there's a logical progression happening.

56
00:02:39,330 --> 00:02:41,070
So that was kind of accidentally

57
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:44,330
we're kind of already dealing with the development of an argument.

58
00:02:44,340 --> 00:02:47,870
But there's another component to this, and that's a little bit more complicated.

59
00:02:47,870 --> 00:02:50,660
And that's probably the hardest challenge I have with you guys today,

60
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:53,960
is to describe the structural view of passages.

61
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:55,620
That'll be the second study.

62
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:58,860
So for each of them, the first one I call it "developing an argument".

63
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:02,660
We're going to do a number of case studies of how arguments are developed

64
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:06,240
through a course of a set of āyāt. How an idea is built upon.

65
00:03:06,250 --> 00:03:08,860
Okay? So we're gonna look at a few passages, a few case studies of that.

66
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,600
Then we're going to take a step back and

67
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,660
look at a structural view of certain passages.

68
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:16,820
How are things organized from a sometimes looks like a symmetrical point of view.

69
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:19,740
Some sort of patterns are established, some connections are made,

70
00:03:19,750 --> 00:03:21,350
and that sounds a bit complicated.

71
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:22,300
But, Inshāllāh ta'āla

72
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:25,200
my job is to try to make that easy to understand and for you to be able

73
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:26,880
to see some of the more sophisticated level

74
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:29,450
of organization in the passages of the Qur'ān.

75
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:32,210
So let's begin first and foremost with a set

76
00:03:32,210 --> 00:03:34,050
of āyāt that belonged to Sūrat al-Baqara.

77
00:03:34,140 --> 00:03:37,720
I'm looking at āyāhs number 91-93.

78
00:03:37,730 --> 00:03:41,500
These, of course, are part of the discourse on the Israelites.

79
00:03:41,510 --> 00:03:46,180
So Sūrat al-Baqara 91-93, and Allāh is criticizing the Israelites.

80
00:03:46,180 --> 00:03:50,214
And here's the criticism
وَإِذَا قِيلَ لَهُمْ ءَامِنُوا۟ بِمَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ

81
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:54,014
When it is said to them, believe in what Allah sent down.

82
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:56,660
قَالُوا۟ نُؤْمِنُ بِمَآ أُنزِلَ عَلَيْنَا

83
00:03:56,740 --> 00:04:01,380
They say, basically, they say we already believe in what was sent to us.

84
00:04:01,380 --> 00:04:04,750
So they are told 'Believe in Qur'ān', They say, 'No thanks. We already have the Tawrāt.'

85
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:06,060
Essentially.

86
00:04:06,540 --> 00:04:08,155
وَيَكْفُرُونَ بِمَا وَرَآءَهُ

87
00:04:08,165 --> 00:04:09,470
While the fact of the matter is,

88
00:04:09,470 --> 00:04:11,760
they actually disbelieve in what they have behind them.

89
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:14,890
Allāh is saying, not only do you not believe in the Qur'ān,

90
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:17,750
I am claiming you don't even believe in Tawrāt.

91
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:22,193
وَيَكْفُرُونَ بِمَا وَرَآءَهُۥ وَهُوَ ٱلْحَقُّ مُصَدِّقًۭا لِّمَا مَعَهُمْ

92
00:04:22,303 --> 00:04:24,150
And it is the truth,

93
00:04:24,150 --> 00:04:27,350
meaning Qur'ān is the truth, confirming what they have with them.

94
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:32,050
Notice the language. It's the truth confirming what they have with them.

95
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:34,430
Not the truth confirming what they believe

96
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:37,350
because they don't believe in it. Allāh is criticizing

97
00:04:37,350 --> 00:04:38,760
you don't even believe in your own Tawrāt

98
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:43,660
as expected. But what you have in your possession, Qur'ān confirms.

99
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:47,533
قُلْ فَلِمَ تَقْتُلُونَ أَنۢبِيَآءَ ٱللَّهِ

100
00:04:47,663 --> 00:04:49,673
Say or basically ask then

101
00:04:49,670 --> 00:04:52,013
why then did you kill or did you engage in

102
00:04:52,050 --> 00:04:55,550
the killing of prophets of Allah [مِن قَبْلُ] from so long ago

103
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:58,890
إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ
if in fact, you are all believers? Remember

104
00:04:58,890 --> 00:05:03,850
I told you maybe in not recorded portion of this discussion. I told you that,

105
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:08,150
they actually killed prophets and justified it in their books.

106
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:12,510
They would describe prophets in many cases ars very despicable people,

107
00:05:12,510 --> 00:05:13,480
very bad people

108
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:14,960
that should be disobeyed.

109
00:05:15,740 --> 00:05:18,230
And that's why the Qur'ān even adds the qualifier:

110
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:20,780
You killed prophets without any right.

111
00:05:20,890 --> 00:05:22,550
(بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ) or (بِغَيْرِ الحَقٍّۢ).

112
00:05:22,940 --> 00:05:25,760
You don't like, Muneer pointed it out, you don't have to (بِغَيْرِ الحَقٍّۢ).

113
00:05:25,770 --> 00:05:27,360
Killing prophets is bad enough.

114
00:05:27,370 --> 00:05:29,560
What does it mean to say you killed prophets without any right?

115
00:05:30,640 --> 00:05:32,160
You had no right to kill prophets.

116
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:34,860
Well, even if you didn't say without any right, it's still wrong.

117
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:39,750
So the the addition without any right is because they claim they did have right.

118
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:44,480
They actually justified it. And Allāh says: No, your justifications are false.

119
00:05:44,490 --> 00:05:47,710
Anyway, so here Allāh asked, Why did you kill the prophets of Allāh

120
00:05:47,690 --> 00:05:50,980
in fact, if you're believers?
وَلَقَدْ جَآءَكُم مُّوسَىٰ بِٱلْبَيِّنَـٰتِ

121
00:05:50,990 --> 00:05:53,320
And Musa certainly came to you with clear proofs.

122
00:05:53,330 --> 00:05:55,114
ثُمَّ ٱتَّخَذْتُمُ ٱلْعِجْلَ مِنۢ بَعْدِهِ

123
00:05:55,139 --> 00:05:59,060
and you there after, even after he came to you with the clearest evidences

124
00:05:59,340 --> 00:06:01,350
you held on to the calf for worship,

125
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:04,870
even after him, وَأَنتُمْ ظَـٰلِمُونَ,
while you were doing wrong.

126
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:07,990
وَإِذْ أَخَذْنَا مِيثَـٰقَكُمْ وَرَفَعْنَا فَوْقَكُمُ ٱلطُّورَ

127
00:06:08,050 --> 00:06:10,210
When We took the covenant from you and

128
00:06:10,210 --> 00:06:12,350
We raised the mountain of at-Tūr above you

129
00:06:12,481 --> 00:06:13,890
خُذُوا۟ مَآ ءَاتَيْنَـٰكُم بِقُوَّةٍۢ

130
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:17,050
hold on to what We have given you with great might.

131
00:06:17,140 --> 00:06:18,920
وَٱسْمَعُوا۟
and listen

132
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:23,860
قَالُوا۟ سَمِعْنَا وَعَصَيْنَا
They said we hear and we disobey

133
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:26,626
وَأُشْرِبُوا۟ فِى قُلُوبِهِمُ ٱلْعِجْلَ بِكُفْرِهِمْ

134
00:06:26,750 --> 00:06:33,326
And thus the the the love of the calf was poured and gulped down their hearts.

135
00:06:33,390 --> 00:06:36,571
Made to gulp down their hearts because of their disbelief.

136
00:06:36,596 --> 00:06:39,460
قُلْ بِئْسَمَا يَأْمُرُكُم بِهِۦٓ إِيمَـٰنُكُمْ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ

137
00:06:39,530 --> 00:06:42,800
Tell them how terrible your faith-this faith of yours,

138
00:06:42,810 --> 00:06:46,160
what terrible things it compels you to do if in fact you are believers.

139
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:50,080
This is the passage, I did not deliberately, as I was translating it

140
00:06:50,090 --> 00:06:53,960
I deliberately tried to not highlight how the argument is progressing.

141
00:06:54,340 --> 00:06:57,250
Because I want to now highlight to you how the argument is progressing.

142
00:06:57,700 --> 00:06:59,430
The first issue brought was

143
00:06:59,550 --> 00:07:01,560
when you're told accept the Qur'ān,

144
00:07:02,340 --> 00:07:03,710
they say "No".

145
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:05,730
Instead of having reverence for the Qur'ān,

146
00:07:05,740 --> 00:07:07,590
we already have reverence for something we have.

147
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:08,250
Which is what?

148
00:07:08,740 --> 00:07:11,040
Tawrāt, and Allāh says: No, you don't.

149
00:07:11,050 --> 00:07:12,630
Even though if you did,

150
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:16,170
you would see that the Qur'ān is confirming what truth you have left in the Tawrāt.

151
00:07:17,140 --> 00:07:19,590
And if you are so regarding of Tawrāt,

152
00:07:19,650 --> 00:07:22,200
how come you killed the prophets who taught the Tawrāt?

153
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:26,680
I--my--Allāh's proof that you don't believe in the Tawrāt

154
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:28,920
is that you justified the killing of the prophets

155
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:31,460
who actually came to reinforce the teachings of the  Tawrāt.

156
00:07:31,470 --> 00:07:33,183
فَلِمَ تَقْتُلُونَ أَنۢبِيَآءَ ٱللَّهِ

157
00:07:33,207 --> 00:07:34,330
إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ

158
00:07:34,615 --> 00:07:39,300
Taurah--You know, the prophets of Banī Isrā'īl would come, not with new revelation.

159
00:07:39,310 --> 00:07:42,150
They would come to restore the Tawrāt given to Musa.

160
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:46,170
And teach it again. And they would hate that and kill them, and corrupt it again.

161
00:07:46,170 --> 00:07:49,060
They'd teach it again, they killed them and corrupt them again.

162
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:52,660
So Allāh says: Fine, you had no respect for the prophets.

163
00:07:52,660 --> 00:07:56,090
But at least the prophet that got you out of the clutches of the Pharaoh.

164
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:59,060
The ones you even-- the إضافة (annexation) they make. We say: كتاب الله (Book of Allāh).

165
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:00,860
We say كتاب الله (book of Allāh)

166
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:03,250
You know what they say?
"Tawrāt Mouche"

167
00:08:04,340 --> 00:08:05,115
"Tawrat Mouche"

168
00:08:05,140 --> 00:08:11,260
What does that mean? The Torah of. So they have reverence at least for Musa.

169
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:14,150
Allāh then progresses the argument further.

170
00:08:14,150 --> 00:08:15,970
You told Me you have reverence for Tawrāt.

171
00:08:16,150 --> 00:08:19,560
I'm telling you, you don't because you even killed the prophets who taught the Tawrāt.

172
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:22,650
Forget the other prophets. You didn't even spare Musa.

173
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:25,460
وَلَقَدْ جَآءَكُم مُّوسَىٰ بِٱلْبَيِّنَـٰتِ

174
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:27,690
Even Musa had come to you with the clearest of proofs .

175
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:30,390
And what did you do with Musa who had given the Tawrāt to you?

176
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:32,159
The original giver of the Tawrāt to you?

177
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:34,559
You started worshiping a calf

178
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:36,659
even in his presence.

179
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:40,049
مِنۢ بَعْدِهِۦ
And you were doing wrong in his face

180
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:41,460
arguing against him.

181
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:44,950
And so now we've seen, okay

182
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:48,190
no regard for the Tawrāt, no regard for the teachers of Tawrāt

183
00:08:48,190 --> 00:08:51,830
historically and no regard for the even their their political hero,

184
00:08:51,830 --> 00:08:54,950
their prophet, the one they identified themselves with; Musa (عليه السلام)

185
00:08:54,980 --> 00:08:56,160
you didn't even regard him.

186
00:08:57,140 --> 00:08:58,470
But the argument is not done.

187
00:08:58,630 --> 00:09:01,850
Let's talk about how much regard you have even for Allāh Himself.

188
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:04,330
Because if you go-- keep going higher up above

189
00:09:04,330 --> 00:09:06,360
the prophets for them is Musa above Musa is who?

190
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:08,371
Allāh 'azwa jal

191
00:09:08,396 --> 00:09:11,040
So Allāh says
وَإِذْ أَخَذْنَا مِيثَـٰقَكُمْ

192
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:15,495
when We ourselves took the covenant from you.
وَرَفَعْنَا فَوْقَكُمُ ٱلطُّورَ

193
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:18,550
We elevated the mountain above your heads.

194
00:09:19,640 --> 00:09:21,140
Allah Himself told you

195
00:09:21,140 --> 00:09:22,412
خُذُوا۟ مَآ ءَاتَيْنَـٰكُم

196
00:09:22,437 --> 00:09:24,552
Hold on to what We've given you with great might.

197
00:09:24,650 --> 00:09:28,332
You even turned to God directly and said
سَمِعْنَا وَعَصَيْنَا

198
00:09:28,862 --> 00:09:30,250
We hear and we disobey.

199
00:09:31,540 --> 00:09:35,010
This is what you're, you say thanks we already believe.

200
00:09:35,010 --> 00:09:37,975
This is where the conversation started and Allāh is saying: Oh,

201
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,160
this is how you believe?

202
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:42,180
What did you do with prophets? What did you Musa?

203
00:09:42,205 --> 00:09:43,585
What did you do with Allāh Himself?

204
00:09:44,640 --> 00:09:46,050
When you spoke with the Allāh directly?

205
00:09:46,830 --> 00:09:51,820
Then
وَأُشْرِبُوا۟ فِى قُلُوبِهِمُ ٱلْعِجْلَ بِكُفْرِهِمْ ۚ

206
00:09:51,950 --> 00:09:55,920
[قُلْ] Tell them after all this, because the conversation started with

207
00:09:56,000 --> 00:10:00,060
نُؤْمِنُ بِمَآ أُنزِلَ عَلَيْنَا
we believe in what was given to us

208
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:04,560
by the end Allāh says, what a terrible thing this faith of yours makes you do

209
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:08,810
what horrible things it tells you to do.
إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ
If in fact, that is faith.

210
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:13,310
If you'd like to call that faith, it's been telling you to do some pretty wild stuff.

211
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:17,860
Killing prophets, disregarding Musa, worshiping a calf, defying Allāh directly.

212
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:21,880
Wow, mā shāʾ Allāh, some good Imān (faith) you got there, essentially

213
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:24,660
بِئْسَمَا يَأْمُرُكُم بِهِۦٓ إِيمَـٰنُكُمْ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ

214
00:10:24,799 --> 00:10:28,360
You see how they're smart answer has been crushed

215
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:30,620
one after the other, after the other,

216
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:33,850
with a progression that gets worse and worse and worse and worse.

217
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:37,395
Okay is that one clear to everybody? Okay so we'll quickly move along Inshallah

218
00:10:37,420 --> 00:10:40,060
this is a brief one, yet an interesting one.

219
00:10:40,540 --> 00:10:44,400
And it's how Ibrahim (عليه السلام) is used as part of progressing an argument.

220
00:10:44,410 --> 00:10:51,680
We're looking at Surāt al-Imrān, and we're looking at āyāt number 64 to 67.

221
00:10:51,690 --> 00:10:53,160
قُلْ يَـٰٓأَهْلَ ٱلْكِتَـٰبِ

222
00:10:53,740 --> 00:10:57,360
Say people of the book
تَعَالَوْا۟ إِلَىٰ كَلِمَةٍۢ

223
00:10:57,840 --> 00:10:59,470
come towards a word

224
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:03,860
سَوَآءٍۭ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمْ
that is in common between you and ourselves.

225
00:11:03,870 --> 00:11:06,070
Why don't you come and let's discuss something

226
00:11:06,070 --> 00:11:09,810
you-- a teaching that both you and ourselves have in common.

227
00:11:09,820 --> 00:11:12,760
Muslims are told to give this invitation to Jews and Christians.

228
00:11:12,770 --> 00:11:17,160
أَلَّا نَعْبُدَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهَ
that we're not gonna worship anyone except God. except Allāh.

229
00:11:17,440 --> 00:11:18,714
وَلَا نُشْرِكَ بِهِۦ شَيْـًۭٔا

230
00:11:18,770 --> 00:11:21,360
And we will not make any partners with Him in any way, shape or form.

231
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:24,290
وَلَا يَتَّخِذَ بَعْضُنَا بَعْضًا أَرْبَابًۭا مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ

232
00:11:24,330 --> 00:11:26,070
And we will not take some of us

233
00:11:26,540 --> 00:11:29,260
as opposed to others as gods besides Allāh.

234
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:32,984
فَإِن تَوَلَّوْا۟
And if they still turn away

235
00:11:33,009 --> 00:11:36,650
فَقُولُوا۟ ٱشْهَدُوا۟ بِأَنَّا مُسْلِمُونَ
then as they turn away, say to them,

236
00:11:36,650 --> 00:11:38,650
At least testify that we're Muslims.

237
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:41,760
At least say with your mouth, You're not Muslim and we are.

238
00:11:42,540 --> 00:11:43,760
Which they would happily say.

239
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:45,350
They'll say, Yeah, fine.

240
00:11:45,740 --> 00:11:46,930
شَهِدْنا أَنْتُمْ مُسْلِمُونَ

241
00:11:47,005 --> 00:11:51,100
Well, we testify you are Muslims. Muslims to them are deviant and wrong anyway.

242
00:11:51,940 --> 00:11:54,960
What does Allāh say next? First, He said, Come to a common word.

243
00:11:55,940 --> 00:11:59,290
And what was the common word? Worship the same God, don't do shirk,

244
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:00,770
don't make false gods, as you know,

245
00:12:00,770 --> 00:12:03,260
deified, popeified kind of entities, things like that.

246
00:12:04,230 --> 00:12:07,160
Then He says:
يَـٰٓأَهْلَ ٱلْكِتَـٰبِ لِمَ تُحَآجُّونَ فِىٓ إِبْرَٰهِيمَ

247
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:10,750
People of the book, why are you even arguing about Abraham?

248
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:13,880
When we say we have something in common with the Jews and the Christians

249
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:17,000
we call it the religion of Abraham, right? The Abrahamic faiths.

250
00:12:17,030 --> 00:12:19,260
That's the term that you may have heard. Allāh then

251
00:12:19,260 --> 00:12:21,510
builds on that idea and says, People of the book

252
00:12:21,520 --> 00:12:24,620
why are you even making arguments about Ibrahim and claiming him?

253
00:12:24,698 --> 00:12:27,860
وَمَآ أُنزِلَتِ ٱلتَّوْرَىٰةُ وَٱلْإِنجِيلُ إِلَّا مِنۢ بَعْدِهِۦٓ

254
00:12:28,540 --> 00:12:30,360
Tawrāt and Injil was only given after him.

255
00:12:31,740 --> 00:12:33,150
That's that's a later thing.

256
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:38,429
Ibrahim (عليه السلام), if you were to look at his legacy, all it amounts to is:

257
00:12:38,454 --> 00:12:45,521
أَلَّا نَعْبُدَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهَ وَلَا نُشْرِكَ بِهِۦ شَيْـًۭٔا وَلَا يَتَّخِذَ بَعْضُنَا بَعْضًا أَرْبَابًۭا مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ ۚ

258
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:48,080
The common word that we started with

259
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:50,360
no one better represents that common word than who?

260
00:12:50,840 --> 00:12:53,180
Ibrahim  (عليه السلام). So why are you even arguing about Ibrahim?

261
00:12:53,190 --> 00:12:54,950
What we're saying is very Abrahamic.

262
00:12:55,740 --> 00:12:56,960
Why do you have a problem with that?

263
00:12:57,840 --> 00:13:01,560
And then أَفَلَا تَعْقِلُونَ
Why don't you- Why don't you then apply your intellect?

264
00:13:01,690 --> 00:13:05,312
هَـٰٓأَنتُمْ هَـٰٓؤُلَآءِ حَـٰجَجْتُمْ فِيمَا لَكُم بِهِۦ عِلْمٌۭ

265
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:09,090
Here you are debating about things that you do know some things about.

266
00:13:09,100 --> 00:13:10,790
We see you debating about Moses.

267
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:13,860
We see you're debating about, you know, Jesus, etc etc.

268
00:13:14,430 --> 00:13:16,800
فَلِمَ تُحَآجُّونَ فِيمَا لَيْسَ لَكُم بِهِۦ عِلْمٌۭ ۚ

269
00:13:16,977 --> 00:13:19,003
Why are you even arguing about stuff, you know nothing of?

270
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:20,960
Why are you even making things up?

271
00:13:21,540 --> 00:13:24,660
Because you know what some Christian theological arguments became?

272
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:27,160
The arguments became that of course, salvation

273
00:13:27,260 --> 00:13:29,450
is only through the blood of Jesus,

274
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:33,120
right? Humanity's sins are paid for through the blood of Jesus.

275
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:37,075
And the only way to save yourself is by accepting Jesus as Lord and Savior.

276
00:13:37,940 --> 00:13:41,860
But you can only accept Jesus as Lord and savior if you came after Jesus.

277
00:13:42,940 --> 00:13:44,260
So what's gonna happen to Abraham?

278
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:46,150
What's gonna happen to Moses?

279
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:48,820
All these people that are talked about in the Bible

280
00:13:49,090 --> 00:13:50,560
that were prophets of God

281
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:53,060
did not have the blood of Jesus to save them.

282
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:56,730
So what's gonna happen with them? Are they going to go to heaven without Jesus?

283
00:13:56,730 --> 00:14:00,030
But wait, if we say they're going to go to heaven without Jesus, that's a problem.

284
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:02,660
Because that then that undercuts our whole Jesus theory.

285
00:14:03,640 --> 00:14:06,500
So we have to come up with a new-- postulate a new theory.

286
00:14:06,510 --> 00:14:09,640
So some denominations of Christianity came up with a solution,

287
00:14:09,650 --> 00:14:13,140
and the solution was that those prophets and those good people that are mentioned

288
00:14:13,140 --> 00:14:16,450
in the Bible from the past are stuck in the elevator called purgatory.

289
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:20,960
Okay? It's a place called Purgatory, it's not quite hell,

290
00:14:21,340 --> 00:14:24,160
it's not heaven. They're basically stuck in the elevator.

291
00:14:24,540 --> 00:14:26,170
And on Judgment Day, Jesus is gonna come.

292
00:14:26,170 --> 00:14:28,350
They're gonna say, Oh, Lord and savior, And then they can go in.

293
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:31,450
So they had to make this up.

294
00:14:31,944 --> 00:14:35,210
Allāh says I see you are arguing about things that are actually revealed

295
00:14:35,210 --> 00:14:36,920
and you change it a little bit, you have some argument.

296
00:14:36,930 --> 00:14:38,160
Why are you making stuff up?

297
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:40,860
Why are you even making these debates?

298
00:14:41,700 --> 00:14:45,231
فَلِمَ تُحَآجُّونَ فِيمَا لَيْسَ لَكُم بِهِۦ عِلْمٌۭ ۚ وَٱللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ وَأَنتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُونَ

299
00:14:45,310 --> 00:14:46,733
Allāh knows and you dont know.

300
00:14:46,940 --> 00:14:52,150
And then finally He uses the Abrahamic legacy to basically make the point:

301
00:14:52,150 --> 00:14:54,950
They were probably saying, Yeah, fine, you're Muslim, we're not.

302
00:14:55,740 --> 00:14:56,225
But Allāh says

303
00:14:56,250 --> 00:15:00,140
by you saying that we are Muslim and you're not. Here is the point.

304
00:15:00,150 --> 00:15:03,053
مَا كَانَ إِبْرَٰهِيمُ يَهُودِيًّۭا وَلَا نَصْرَانِيًّۭا

305
00:15:03,343 --> 00:15:07,097
Ibrahim (عليه السلام) was neither Jewish nor Christian

306
00:15:07,267 --> 00:15:08,910
وَلَـٰكِن كَانَ حَنِيفًۭا مُّسْلِمًۭا

307
00:15:08,910 --> 00:15:11,830
however he was solely focused before Allāh,

308
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:14,060
one who submits to the will of God 'a Muslim'.

309
00:15:15,340 --> 00:15:16,757
وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ ٱلْمُشْرِكِينَ

310
00:15:16,877 --> 00:15:19,620
And he did not commit any form of shirk. He did not commit adultery--

311
00:15:19,630 --> 00:15:22,923
you know idolatory of any kind. What is the āyāh saying?

312
00:15:23,053 --> 00:15:28,988
By calling us Muslim, you are calling us those who uphold the legacy of Abraham.

313
00:15:29,013 --> 00:15:31,890
By saying-- by you calling us Muslim

314
00:15:31,900 --> 00:15:36,670
you've actually handed over the license to carry the legacy of Ibrahim to us.

315
00:15:36,670 --> 00:15:38,410
You no longer have the right to that legacy.

316
00:15:38,420 --> 00:15:40,490
You don't get to say you are loyal to Ibrahim.

317
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:42,460
You don't get to say you are Abrahamic faiths now.

318
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:46,290
So that's how the argument has progressed from Islam to Ibrahim.

319
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:48,860
And those two things have been tied together. Okay?

320
00:15:49,940 --> 00:15:53,070
That's our second case study. Now we're gonna switch gears.

321
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:56,910
Those were Meccan examples, and we're going to go to

322
00:15:56,920 --> 00:16:02,420
a progressive argument in Surat an-Naba, Makki surah, 78.

323
00:16:02,430 --> 00:16:07,390
And we're gonna look at āyāhs number 6 all the way to 16.

324
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:09,350
Okay? These are āyāt of creation.

325
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:11,170
I'll translate them first for you,

326
00:16:11,170 --> 00:16:14,160
and then show you some imagery and the progression of imagery in the āyāt.

327
00:16:14,540 --> 00:16:16,119
أَلَمْ نَجْعَلِ ٱلْأَرْضَ مِهَـٰدًۭا

328
00:16:16,219 --> 00:16:18,160
Didn't We make the earth into a cradle?

329
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:20,620
وَٱلْجِبَالَ أَوْتَادًۭا

330
00:16:20,860 --> 00:16:23,560
And didn't We make the mountains into pegs?

331
00:16:24,140 --> 00:16:26,860
أَوْتَادًۭا - is used for the pegs you put down for a tent.

332
00:16:28,340 --> 00:16:30,200
وَخَلَقْنَـٰكُمْ أَزْوَٰجًۭا

333
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:32,660
And didn't We--and We made you into spouses.

334
00:16:33,361 --> 00:16:34,880
وَجَعَلْنَا نَوْمَكُمْ سُبَاتًۭا

335
00:16:34,880 --> 00:16:37,488
And We made your sleep into something that cuts you off.

336
00:16:37,688 --> 00:16:39,660
يعني قطعا سباتا قطعا

337
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,488
It cuts you off

338
00:16:41,545 --> 00:16:45,488
وَجَعَلْنَا ٱلَّيْلَ لِبَاسًۭا
And We made the night into a garment, a clothing.

339
00:16:45,513 --> 00:16:49,760
وَجَعَلْنَا ٱلنَّهَارَ مَعَاشًۭا
And We made the day into a means of living.

340
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:54,900
وَبَنَيْنَا فَوْقَكُمْ سَبْعًۭا شِدَادًۭا
And We placed above you

341
00:16:54,900 --> 00:16:57,360
seven intense ones, meaning seven skies.

342
00:16:57,740 --> 00:17:02,660
وَجَعَلْنَا سِرَاجًۭا وَهَّاجًۭا
And We placed a burning lamp,

343
00:17:03,640 --> 00:17:06,270
a brilliant blazing lamp, meaning referring to the sun.

344
00:17:06,640 --> 00:17:09,890
وَأَنزَلْنَا مِنَ ٱلْمُعْصِرَٰتِ مَآءًۭ ثَجَّاجًۭا

345
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:13,900
And We sent down from the squeezing clouds water that gushes out

346
00:17:13,925 --> 00:17:18,119
لِّنُخْرِجَ بِهِۦ حَبًّۭا وَنَبَاتًۭا
وَجَنَّـٰتٍ أَلْفَافًا

347
00:17:18,219 --> 00:17:24,130
So that by means of it grains and produce can come out and gardens that are lush can come forth.

348
00:17:24,140 --> 00:17:28,270
Okay, so these are āyāt of Allāh from the earth, the mountain and so on and so forth.

349
00:17:28,270 --> 00:17:28,660
Okay?

350
00:17:29,140 --> 00:17:31,840
You'll notice in these āyāt, there's an imagery

351
00:17:31,970 --> 00:17:32,860
that's been captured.

352
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:39,050
Surāt an-Naba's function, its basic premise is there's a life after death.

353
00:17:39,540 --> 00:17:40,670
Judgment Day is coming.

354
00:17:41,140 --> 00:17:43,280
And everything Allāh makes is in pairs.

355
00:17:43,530 --> 00:17:46,380
This life has been paired with the next one.

356
00:17:46,580 --> 00:17:48,960
Jannah has been paired with Nār (fire), for example.

357
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:51,200
This life is like one day,

358
00:17:51,210 --> 00:17:53,430
because when people will rise on Judgment Day and they

359
00:17:53,430 --> 00:17:55,020
will be asked how long did you stay here?

360
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:55,660
What will they say?

361
00:17:55,820 --> 00:17:58,380
لَبِثْنَا يَوْمًا

362
00:17:58,530 --> 00:17:59,460
We were only here for a day.

363
00:17:59,940 --> 00:18:00,450
Okay?

364
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:02,960
And this day has been paired with that day.

365
00:18:03,740 --> 00:18:05,560
This day and that day. Okay?

366
00:18:06,040 --> 00:18:08,460
Allāh says this function or this design of Allāh

367
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:11,170
of things in pairs, Allāh put in everything.

368
00:18:11,740 --> 00:18:13,820
And so what-- part of that is

369
00:18:13,830 --> 00:18:16,930
the earth is paired and earth Allah actually

370
00:18:16,930 --> 00:18:19,270
paired with the flat land with the mountain.

371
00:18:20,040 --> 00:18:24,910
The earth is 'مِهَـٰدًۭا' and the 'ٱلْجِبَالَ' is 'أَوْتَادًۭا' Okay?

372
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:29,810
And this is actually also goes into a subtle bit of imagery,

373
00:18:29,820 --> 00:18:31,160
things alluding to other things.

374
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:32,270
'مِهَـٰدًۭا' is a bed,

375
00:18:33,040 --> 00:18:35,490
but 'مِهَـٰدًۭا' is also the womb of a mother, mahad.

376
00:18:35,830 --> 00:18:37,360
The cradle of a mother.

377
00:18:37,940 --> 00:18:40,460
The earth is being described as a motherly,

378
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:45,650
you know image. And the earth has the same qualities as a mother. How so?

379
00:18:45,660 --> 00:18:48,820
Because the earth produces life, like a mother produces life.

380
00:18:48,820 --> 00:18:49,960
The female produces life.

381
00:18:50,540 --> 00:18:55,320
The mountain is a symbol of strength, stability. What is this supposed to be? The man's role.

382
00:18:55,410 --> 00:18:56,170
Qawwām.

383
00:18:56,640 --> 00:18:57,360
Stable.

384
00:18:57,940 --> 00:19:00,850
So the female and the male are compared like the earth and

385
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:04,270
the mountain. And of course, the mountain is described as,

386
00:19:04,840 --> 00:19:05,950
(أَوْتَادًۭا) pegged.

387
00:19:06,640 --> 00:19:09,840
And the peg is supposed to be something that stays in place, offers stability.

388
00:19:09,850 --> 00:19:10,670
Okay?

389
00:19:10,680 --> 00:19:12,390
Which is why I-- one of the reasons

390
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:15,160
rijāl are called rijāl, it is from rijal. And what is rijal?

391
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:18,340
They have their foot firm on the ground.

392
00:19:18,350 --> 00:19:21,980
They are on firm standing; as part of the implication of the word the rijāl.

393
00:19:21,990 --> 00:19:22,760
Okay?

394
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:23,860
Now

395
00:19:24,340 --> 00:19:27,870
the progression here is also--Neil Robinson said this so beautifully

396
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:30,460
in his work on this surāh.

397
00:19:31,340 --> 00:19:32,350
He describes

398
00:19:32,490 --> 00:19:34,270
think of all of this imagery

399
00:19:34,740 --> 00:19:35,850
as someone on a journey.

400
00:19:36,940 --> 00:19:37,960
Someone on a journey.

401
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:40,670
They're traveling in the journey

402
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:41,950
in the desert.

403
00:19:42,110 --> 00:19:43,050
What's their bed?

404
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:44,950
The earth.

405
00:19:45,940 --> 00:19:48,850
And then they're going to set up a tent as night comes.

406
00:19:50,240 --> 00:19:54,260
But they see the entire earth is a bed. And what looks like tents?

407
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:56,050
The mountains do.

408
00:19:57,040 --> 00:20:00,310
And now, Allāh says, Just like the earth and the mountains are paired,

409
00:20:00,330 --> 00:20:01,450
you're also paired.

410
00:20:02,540 --> 00:20:04,160
And now imagine night falls

411
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:07,600
because he's traveling and night has fallen. He's going to set up his tent.

412
00:20:07,870 --> 00:20:10,350
And he's going to sleep next to his spouse.

413
00:20:10,470 --> 00:20:13,380
وَجَعَلْنَا نَوْمَكُمْ سُبَاتًۭا

414
00:20:13,740 --> 00:20:16,200
and then He says, the night has been made--

415
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:19,190
Now the night has fallen because sleep logically leads into night.

416
00:20:19,340 --> 00:20:22,480
The night has fallen and the night He describes as لِبَاسًۭا

417
00:20:22,490 --> 00:20:25,050
which is really interesting because the only other time in the Qurān

418
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:26,570
spouse

419
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:28,360
and لِبَاسًۭا come together

420
00:20:28,940 --> 00:20:30,260
are in the āyāt of Ramadan.

421
00:20:31,260 --> 00:20:34,553
هُنَّ لِبَاسٌۭ لَّكُمْ وَأَنتُمْ لِبَاسٌۭ لَّهُنَّ

422
00:20:34,680 --> 00:20:37,860
The night was made into a garment, just like your spouse is made into a garment.

423
00:20:38,430 --> 00:20:41,270
Speaking of spouse, the night is also a garment. It's like that.

424
00:20:42,040 --> 00:20:44,950
Okay, just like your spouses, your garment. The night is also a garment.

425
00:20:45,340 --> 00:20:50,170
Now, after the night is done
وَجَعَلْنَا ٱلنَّهَارَ مَعَاشًۭا
night is over

426
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:52,360
time to get up and make a living.

427
00:20:53,040 --> 00:20:55,770
And when he makes a living, he's going to roll up his tent

428
00:20:56,440 --> 00:20:57,360
and he's going to get out.

429
00:20:57,740 --> 00:21:00,110
The sun in the desert is open and intense.

430
00:21:00,110 --> 00:21:01,126
So what's he going to notice?

431
00:21:01,151 --> 00:21:04,850
وَبَنَيْنَا فَوْقَكُمْ سَبْعًۭا شِدَادًۭا
The seven skies above him

432
00:21:05,240 --> 00:21:07,550
and in that sky, what's the most prominent thing?

433
00:21:07,831 --> 00:21:09,400
وَجَعَلْنَا سِرَاجًۭا وَهَّاجًۭا

434
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:14,450
The intense burning sun. That intense burning sun can also be a kind of death.

435
00:21:15,340 --> 00:21:16,820
But Allāh brings relief,

436
00:21:16,830 --> 00:21:18,830
not only does He bring that intense burning lamp

437
00:21:18,887 --> 00:21:21,500
وَأَنزَلْنَا مِنَ ٱلْمُعْصِرَٰتِ مَآءًۭ ثَجَّاجًۭا

438
00:21:21,525 --> 00:21:24,960
What He brings from that same sky
that is so intense with that burning lamp

439
00:21:24,970 --> 00:21:27,870
He brings clouds that squeeze and water comes down and

440
00:21:27,870 --> 00:21:30,970
then gardens come forth and your your life is sustained.

441
00:21:30,980 --> 00:21:32,770
Everything is moving with everything else.

442
00:21:32,770 --> 00:21:36,640
And Robinson argues that it's, which is even other part of other coherence.

443
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:38,570
where we talked about the placement of passages

444
00:21:38,580 --> 00:21:40,460
that basically what Allāh is saying here

445
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:44,560
is that your life in this world is like one traveler in the desert.

446
00:21:46,279 --> 00:21:49,730
Who goes, sleeps the night, puts his tent down.

447
00:21:49,740 --> 00:21:52,880
Then he's gonna get up and he's gonna roll up his tent and he's gonna go along.

448
00:21:52,880 --> 00:21:54,050
And his eventual destination

449
00:21:54,050 --> 00:21:56,960
might be a garden, just like yours is meant to be the garden of Jannah.

450
00:21:58,040 --> 00:22:03,070
Right? And which is why you'll find in Surat an-Naba

451
00:22:03,270 --> 00:22:05,470
the mountains are gonna sail away

452
00:22:05,470 --> 00:22:07,670
like the tent gets rolled up and taken away,

453
00:22:07,680 --> 00:22:11,400
and the sky is gonna open up like everything is going to move from its place,

454
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:13,170
just like a traveler just moves on.

455
00:22:13,840 --> 00:22:14,800
You know?

456
00:22:15,150 --> 00:22:19,060
So that's the progression of imagery in Surat an-Naba.

457
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:22,700
My favorite example of this, however, is this one.

458
00:22:22,700 --> 00:22:25,130
I don't know if I'll get to do both of them, but I'll do at least one of them.

459
00:22:25,140 --> 00:22:29,040
And that--this is in Sūrat an-Nahl, Sūrah number 16

460
00:22:29,040 --> 00:22:32,550
one of the most profound Sūrahs of imagery I've ever come across.

461
00:22:32,940 --> 00:22:36,600
And this is āyahs number 64 to 69.

462
00:22:36,610 --> 00:22:37,840
I'm going to read these off to you

463
00:22:37,840 --> 00:22:40,310
in translation without showing you the progression first.

464
00:22:40,320 --> 00:22:42,060
And then we'll talk about how they progress.

465
00:22:43,350 --> 00:22:46,060
64 to 69 of Sūrat al-Nahl

466
00:22:46,085 --> 00:22:47,560
al-Nahl is 16, okay?

467
00:22:48,040 --> 00:22:52,450
وَمَآ أَنزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ ٱلْكِتَـٰبَ
We did not send the book down onto you

468
00:22:53,470 --> 00:22:56,405
إِلَّا لِتُبَيِّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلَّذِى ٱخْتَلَفُوا۟ فِيهِ

469
00:22:56,530 --> 00:23:00,845
except that you should clarify for them the things that they disagree about

470
00:23:00,990 --> 00:23:02,465
وَهُدًۭى
and as a guidance,

471
00:23:02,495 --> 00:23:03,932
وَرَحْمَةًۭ
and as a mercy

472
00:23:03,957 --> 00:23:06,572
لِّقَوْمٍۢ يُؤْمِنُونَ
for a group of people that wish to believe.

473
00:23:08,340 --> 00:23:14,110
وَٱللَّهُ أَنزَلَ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءًۭ
And Allāh, He sent down water from the sky

474
00:23:14,490 --> 00:23:17,700
فَأَحْيَا بِهِ ٱلْأَرْضَ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَآ
and by means of the water

475
00:23:17,710 --> 00:23:21,960
He brought earth--life to the earth after its death.

476
00:23:22,340 --> 00:23:25,050
إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَـَٔايَةًۭ لِّقَوْمٍۢ يَسْمَعُونَ.

477
00:23:25,050 --> 00:23:29,250
Certainly there is a sign in that for people that are willing to listen, that are trying to listen.

478
00:23:29,840 --> 00:23:32,282
وَإِنَّ لَكُمْ فِى ٱلْأَنْعَـٰمِ لَعِبْرَةًۭ

479
00:23:32,307 --> 00:23:37,210
And in cattle there is yet another great profound lesson for you.

480
00:23:37,220 --> 00:23:38,660
In what is there a lesson for you?

481
00:23:39,380 --> 00:23:40,140
In cattle.

482
00:23:40,500 --> 00:23:45,030
نُّسْقِيكُم مِّمَّا فِى بُطُونِهِ
We give you drink from what is found in its belly

483
00:23:45,260 --> 00:23:49,100
مِنۢ بَيْنِ فَرْثٍۢ وَدَمٍۢ
from between feces and blood

484
00:23:49,940 --> 00:23:53,000
لَّبَنًا خَالِصًۭا سَآئِغًۭا لِّلشَّـٰرِبِينَ

485
00:23:53,080 --> 00:23:56,560
pure milk that replenishes, rejuvenates those who drink.

486
00:23:57,140 --> 00:23:58,950
وَمِن ثَمَرَٰتِ ٱلنَّخِيلِ

487
00:23:58,960 --> 00:24:01,484
And from the fruits that come from palm trees

488
00:24:01,524 --> 00:24:04,514
وَٱلْأَعْنَـٰبِ
and from grapes

489
00:24:04,634 --> 00:24:10,060
تَتَّخِذُونَ مِنْهُ سَكَرًۭا وَرِزْقًا حَسَنًا ۗ
you use it to produce wine

490
00:24:10,940 --> 00:24:13,160
and good sustenance too.

491
00:24:13,840 --> 00:24:14,640
He separates them.

492
00:24:14,640 --> 00:24:17,860
You can do two things with grapes and with dates, you can make wine out of them

493
00:24:18,240 --> 00:24:20,460
or you can make good stuff from them too.

494
00:24:20,840 --> 00:24:22,370
Because 'سَكَرًۭا' would not be a good thing.

495
00:24:22,380 --> 00:24:24,019
But He says you can make it.

496
00:24:24,043 --> 00:24:27,509
إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَـَٔايَةًۭ لِّقَوْمٍۢ يَعْقِلُونَ

497
00:24:27,499 --> 00:24:32,029
And in all of that, there's certainly a sign for a group of people that are trying to understand.

498
00:24:32,059 --> 00:24:34,160
وَأَوْحَىٰ رَبُّكَ إِلَى ٱلنَّحْلِ

499
00:24:34,540 --> 00:24:36,690
and your Master revealed to the bee

500
00:24:37,440 --> 00:24:39,541
أَنِ ٱتَّخِذِى مِنَ ٱلْجِبَالِ بُيُوتًۭا

501
00:24:39,651 --> 00:24:43,381
that you should take from the mountains--take up homes in the mountains

502
00:24:43,500 --> 00:24:46,100
وَمِنَ ٱلشَّجَرِ
and take up homes in the trees.

503
00:24:46,154 --> 00:24:48,511
وَمِمَّا يَعْرِشُونَ
and from whatever they build

504
00:24:48,601 --> 00:24:53,670
meaning sometimes honey bees build a hive even in in the the columns of a palace

505
00:24:54,040 --> 00:24:58,400
what people built. So not only in nature, in even artificial places

506
00:24:58,460 --> 00:25:00,238
they might end up building something.

507
00:25:00,263 --> 00:25:04,000
ثُمَّ كُلِى مِن كُلِّ ٱلثَّمَرَٰتِ
Then eat from all of the fruits.

508
00:25:04,080 --> 00:25:09,470
فَٱسْلُكِى سُبُلَ رَبِّكِ
Then pursue the pathways identified by your Master

509
00:25:09,840 --> 00:25:11,770
ذُلُلًۭا
with humility

510
00:25:12,621 --> 00:25:16,560
يَخْرُجُ مِنۢ بُطُونِهَا شَرَابٌۭ مُّخْتَلِفٌ أَلْوَٰنُهُ

511
00:25:16,670 --> 00:25:18,569
what comes from its bellies.

512
00:25:18,569 --> 00:25:21,790
Meaning the bellies of the bees is a drink that is of different colors.

513
00:25:21,930 --> 00:25:23,160
He's referring to what drink?

514
00:25:23,640 --> 00:25:25,249
He's referring to honey.

515
00:25:25,289 --> 00:25:28,999
فِيهِ شِفَآءٌۭ لِّلنَّاسِ
in which there is healing for people

516
00:25:29,110 --> 00:25:32,039
إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَـَٔايَةًۭ لِّقَوْمٍۢ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ

517
00:25:32,069 --> 00:25:36,718
In all of that, there certainly is a miraculous sign for people that think deeply.

518
00:25:36,768 --> 00:25:38,960
Okay so this was the passage that

519
00:25:39,340 --> 00:25:43,480
you may have thought of some parallels. Maybe you can guess

520
00:25:43,490 --> 00:25:45,460
what connects these Ayāt? What is it?

521
00:25:46,140 --> 00:25:46,770
Drinks.

522
00:25:47,440 --> 00:25:49,110
Water from the sky.

523
00:25:49,320 --> 00:25:50,260
Milk.

524
00:25:50,940 --> 00:25:51,810
Wine.

525
00:25:52,120 --> 00:25:54,660
Juices, honey, isn't it?

526
00:25:55,140 --> 00:25:56,820
But there's something more going on here.

527
00:25:56,830 --> 00:25:59,480
I deliberately included ayāh number 64 as

528
00:25:59,480 --> 00:26:01,470
the first ayāh of the progressive passage,

529
00:26:01,480 --> 00:26:03,080
which was not about drinks at all.

530
00:26:03,090 --> 00:26:03,960
What is it about?

531
00:26:05,240 --> 00:26:08,960
It's about revelation coming down so you could describe revelation to people.

532
00:26:09,540 --> 00:26:13,480
And revelation will serve as guidance and revelation will serve as mercy

533
00:26:13,610 --> 00:26:15,170
for people that seek to believe.

534
00:26:15,540 --> 00:26:18,080
Everything else that follows is imagery that

535
00:26:18,080 --> 00:26:20,960
will further your understanding of revelation itself.

536
00:26:21,840 --> 00:26:24,600
The imagery are lessons by which we will learn something

537
00:26:24,600 --> 00:26:27,360
about the process of revelation and the effect that it has.

538
00:26:27,940 --> 00:26:31,860
Allāh says, He sent water from the sky and it gave life to the earth.

539
00:26:33,040 --> 00:26:35,110
Just like revelation comes from the sky

540
00:26:35,740 --> 00:26:37,170
and gives life to the hearts.

541
00:26:38,340 --> 00:26:40,460
And usually when water comes from the sky

542
00:26:41,540 --> 00:26:44,500
and gives life to the earth, is that a sign for your ears?

543
00:26:44,510 --> 00:26:46,010
Or is that a sign for your eyes?

544
00:26:47,440 --> 00:26:50,478
That's a sign for your eyes. Look at the end of the āyāh:

545
00:26:50,508 --> 00:26:54,550
إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَـَٔايَةًۭ لِّقَوْمٍۢ يَسْمَعُونَ

546
00:26:55,240 --> 00:26:58,270
In it, there's a sign for people that are trying to listen.

547
00:26:58,740 --> 00:26:59,230
Wait,

548
00:26:59,400 --> 00:27:02,360
which of the signs is for listening? Revelation or water?

549
00:27:04,040 --> 00:27:05,560
So it's talking about revelation.

550
00:27:06,840 --> 00:27:08,850
It's making you think, Look at water

551
00:27:09,340 --> 00:27:10,410
but listen carefully

552
00:27:10,410 --> 00:27:13,960
am I talking really about water, or am I using water as a metaphor?

553
00:27:14,440 --> 00:27:15,460
Subḥānahu wataʿālā.

554
00:27:15,940 --> 00:27:20,670
To describe what what revelation does. What life it brings.

555
00:27:21,540 --> 00:27:24,170
And He says,
speaking of drinks that replenish you

556
00:27:24,220 --> 00:27:26,270
وَإِنَّ لَكُمْ فِى ٱلْأَنْعَـٰمِ لَعِبْرَةًۭ

557
00:27:26,270 --> 00:27:29,100
Yet another parable is you can take a good look

558
00:27:29,100 --> 00:27:31,670
at cattle. Because drink doesn't just come from the sky.

559
00:27:32,140 --> 00:27:33,360
There are other drinks you enjoy.

560
00:27:33,740 --> 00:27:34,850
Like milk.

561
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:39,010
Where does it come from? From the belly of an animal in between

562
00:27:39,010 --> 00:27:41,050
what two things did He specifically say?

563
00:27:41,740 --> 00:27:43,660
Blood and feces. Okay.

564
00:27:44,340 --> 00:27:46,460
The earth can be brought to life.

565
00:27:47,140 --> 00:27:48,360
Something good comes from it.

566
00:27:49,040 --> 00:27:52,060
Now keep that imagery in mind, something good and something pure coming.

567
00:27:52,540 --> 00:27:54,850
The Ṣaḥāba were in a good environment or in a bad environment?

568
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:58,160
They were in one of the worst environments in the world.

569
00:27:59,340 --> 00:28:05,160
They were surrounded with what you can call impurity and impurity, blood and feces.

570
00:28:05,740 --> 00:28:09,130
But when Allāh inspires, then purity can even come from within

571
00:28:09,130 --> 00:28:11,350
the most impure of environments.

572
00:28:13,240 --> 00:28:16,270
The most impure of environments will produce that which will replenish you

573
00:28:16,420 --> 00:28:17,460
and give you.

574
00:28:17,840 --> 00:28:21,190
The Qur'ān is also described as though it came from

575
00:28:21,190 --> 00:28:24,170
the command of Allāh in the most corrupt of environments

576
00:28:24,180 --> 00:28:26,010
and it to this day, it replenishes people.

577
00:28:26,040 --> 00:28:28,550
خَالِصًۭا سَآئِغًۭا لِّلشَّـٰرِبِينَ

578
00:28:29,240 --> 00:28:31,780
Yet another parable for revelation is

579
00:28:31,780 --> 00:28:33,270
that even in the worst of environments,

580
00:28:33,270 --> 00:28:35,370
revelation can come as pure and not be corrupted.

581
00:28:36,040 --> 00:28:38,560
And it will replenish those even if they're in a bad environment.

582
00:28:38,940 --> 00:28:39,860
You with me so far?

583
00:28:40,240 --> 00:28:45,670
Okay, so now we're not just saying revelation is beneficial for you know, yes,

584
00:28:45,670 --> 00:28:47,300
it gives the dead earth life.

585
00:28:47,310 --> 00:28:49,770
But even in a bad environment, it can reform the environment.

586
00:28:50,640 --> 00:28:51,660
He takes the next step,

587
00:28:52,240 --> 00:28:57,460
He says, now ponder over the fruits that come from palm trees and grapes.

588
00:28:58,040 --> 00:29:00,750
But when He talked about them, He didn't just say good stuff comes from it.

589
00:29:00,750 --> 00:29:01,760
What did He say?

590
00:29:03,340 --> 00:29:06,270
Bad stuff comes from it and-- 'سَكَرًۭا'

591
00:29:06,840 --> 00:29:08,960
and you-- He didn't say Allah takes it out. He says

592
00:29:09,100 --> 00:29:11,360
تَتَّخِذُونَ مِنْهُ سَكَرًۭا

593
00:29:11,840 --> 00:29:13,790
you bring out from it wine

594
00:29:14,120 --> 00:29:15,860
and you bring out good 'رِزْقًا' also.

595
00:29:16,740 --> 00:29:20,270
One parable was a bad environment and goods coming out of it. Yes?

596
00:29:21,060 --> 00:29:22,250
The opposite scene.

597
00:29:22,450 --> 00:29:26,060
There's good originally. What's good originally? A palm tree is good

598
00:29:26,190 --> 00:29:28,560
grapes are good. But what's coming out of it?

599
00:29:29,240 --> 00:29:29,770
Bad.

600
00:29:30,240 --> 00:29:34,270
Compare--Understand that the people that were given revelation before us,

601
00:29:34,310 --> 00:29:35,760
the Israelites,

602
00:29:36,340 --> 00:29:39,490
they were given a lot of good. Lots of prophets, the Tawrāt

603
00:29:39,500 --> 00:29:43,350
everything about what they had was good. They took that pure good

604
00:29:43,360 --> 00:29:45,970
and did they use it correctly or incorrectly?

605
00:29:45,980 --> 00:29:48,420
They could have used it as رِزْقًا حَسَنًا

606
00:29:48,430 --> 00:29:51,060
but they turned it into 'سَكَرًۭا' instead.

607
00:29:51,440 --> 00:29:53,655
It's no accident that this Sūrat al-Nahl

608
00:29:53,680 --> 00:29:57,350
at the very end is going to criticize the Israelites, even though it's a Makki Sūrah.

609
00:29:58,540 --> 00:29:58,860
Okay?

610
00:29:59,540 --> 00:30:01,360
You can misuse revelation too.

611
00:30:01,740 --> 00:30:05,060
You can misuse the pure 'رِزْقًا' that Allāh gives you also.

612
00:30:06,240 --> 00:30:10,490
In the worst of environments, purity can be retained.

613
00:30:10,500 --> 00:30:13,860
And in the best of environments, your corruption can make it corrupt too.

614
00:30:14,540 --> 00:30:18,070
تَتَّخِذُونَ مِنْهُ سَكَرًۭا وَرِزْقًا حَسَنًا

615
00:30:18,140 --> 00:30:19,960
And this is for those who really think about it.

616
00:30:21,340 --> 00:30:24,660
Every drink has some reference to what happens with revelations so far. Yeah?

617
00:30:25,740 --> 00:30:27,360
وَأَوْحَىٰ رَبُّكَ إِلَى ٱلنَّحْلِ

618
00:30:27,840 --> 00:30:29,850
Allāh revealed to the bee

619
00:30:30,240 --> 00:30:32,760
and the bees job is to take from different places

620
00:30:33,140 --> 00:30:36,580
and then take pathways that Allāh commanded it to, just like angels

621
00:30:36,580 --> 00:30:39,460
take the pathways Allāh command them to, to deliver revelation.

622
00:30:39,940 --> 00:30:42,160
And Allāh inspired them to bring that revelation.

623
00:30:42,170 --> 00:30:46,400
And when they bring that revelation, what is the benefit of this revelation?

624
00:30:46,490 --> 00:30:48,360
Does revelation have different textures by the way?

625
00:30:48,940 --> 00:30:51,090
Do some Ayāt bring mercy?  Do some bring fear?

626
00:30:51,090 --> 00:30:53,950
Do some bring council? Do some bring knowledge? Do some bring wisdom?

627
00:30:54,440 --> 00:30:56,770
شَرَابٌۭ مُّخْتَلِفٌ أَلْوَٰنُهُۥ

628
00:30:57,140 --> 00:31:00,460
Do all the Sūrahs have the same color? The same texture? The same flavor?

629
00:31:00,840 --> 00:31:03,770
Do they all have their own sweetness? Unique signatures?

630
00:31:04,540 --> 00:31:05,850
And so He says,

631
00:31:05,875 --> 00:31:10,020
فِيهِ شِفَآءٌۭ لِّلنَّاسِ
In it, meaning in honey, there is

632
00:31:10,468 --> 00:31:14,390
healing for people. The only other time 'شِفَآءٌ' is used in the Qur'ān

633
00:31:15,740 --> 00:31:20,538
قَدْ جَآءَتْكُم مَّوْعِظَةٌۭ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ وَشِفَآءٌۭ لِّمَا فِى ٱلصُّدُورِ

634
00:31:20,618 --> 00:31:22,288
Qur'ān is 'شِفَآءٌۭ', honey is 'شِفَآءٌۭ'

635
00:31:22,313 --> 00:31:24,860
because the honey is a parable for the Qur'ān and its sweetness

636
00:31:25,840 --> 00:31:27,060
and its divine origin.

637
00:31:27,940 --> 00:31:31,710
And the way that the honey is extracted,

638
00:31:31,710 --> 00:31:34,060
nobody can extract it except by the command of Allāh.

639
00:31:34,940 --> 00:31:38,040
Its sources and the way it's turned into revelation.

640
00:31:38,050 --> 00:31:41,270
You know like Allāh took, literally, what is right in front of us.

641
00:31:41,270 --> 00:31:42,260
History is in front of us.

642
00:31:42,260 --> 00:31:44,490
The events are in front of us,
and Allāh will make reference to events

643
00:31:44,490 --> 00:31:46,440
that happened before the Prophet's eyes, before the

644
00:31:46,440 --> 00:31:49,920
people's eyes. Allāh will make reference to things that happen in the time of Fir'own

645
00:31:49,930 --> 00:31:51,660
and historians will talk about it.

646
00:31:51,670 --> 00:31:53,450
Others will talk about it, it's the same fruit

647
00:31:53,460 --> 00:31:57,460
but when the honeybee extracts from it and by Allāh's command produces honey,

648
00:31:57,840 --> 00:31:59,670
it's a different thing altogether.

649
00:32:00,440 --> 00:32:04,520
And so it's the same events that a historian sees, that human being sees.

650
00:32:04,530 --> 00:32:06,610
But when Allāh comments on that event,

651
00:32:06,620 --> 00:32:08,860
then its sweetness and its guidance is something else,

652
00:32:08,860 --> 00:32:10,110
it's healing for people

653
00:32:10,135 --> 00:32:12,990
إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَـَٔايَةًۭ لِّقَوْمٍۢ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ

654
00:32:13,110 --> 00:32:15,610
You can go to the same flower that the honeybee goes to.

655
00:32:15,620 --> 00:32:20,170
You can go to the same fruit that the honeybee goes to, and you won't get honey out of it.

656
00:32:21,240 --> 00:32:23,890
That can only happen when Allah extracts from it

657
00:32:23,890 --> 00:32:26,760
by Allāh's command and compiles it.

658
00:32:27,640 --> 00:32:31,740
And so:
إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَـَٔايَةًۭ لِّقَوْمٍۢ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ

659
00:32:32,140 --> 00:32:36,600
So the the the physical imagery in the Qur'ān and sometimes the

660
00:32:36,600 --> 00:32:40,310
way it progresses has some very profound spiritual lessons associated with it.

661
00:32:40,320 --> 00:32:43,840
Okay? Since you guys are doing okay, can I do another one

662
00:32:43,960 --> 00:32:45,550
before the break? Okay.

663
00:32:46,540 --> 00:32:47,801
This is also Sūrat al-Nahl

664
00:32:47,826 --> 00:32:50,260
because I'm obsessed with Sūrat al-Nahl. It's really sweet.

665
00:32:50,840 --> 00:33:05,860
Okay, that's a good one. Yeah, I've tickled myself. Hold on, I-- regain my composure.

666
00:33:08,351 --> 00:33:12,327
بسم الله و الصلاة و السلام على رسول الله و على آله و صحبه أجمعين

667
00:33:12,352 --> 00:33:13,800
أعوذ بالله من الشيطان الرجيم

668
00:33:13,869 --> 00:33:17,483
وَٱللَّهُ أَخْرَجَكُم مِّنۢ بُطُونِ
أُمَّهَـٰتِكُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُونَ شَيْـًۭٔا

669
00:33:17,507 --> 00:33:21,599
وَجَعَلَ لَكُمُ ٱلسَّمْعَ وَٱلْأَبْصَـٰرَ
وَٱلْأَفْـِٔدَةَ ۙ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ

670
00:33:22,940 --> 00:33:25,990
These Ayāt from Sūrat al-Nahl and also represent

671
00:33:25,990 --> 00:33:29,040
a progressive imagery that teaches a profound lesson

672
00:33:29,040 --> 00:33:32,060
about the mercy of Allāh on human beings and how He cares for them.

673
00:33:32,540 --> 00:33:36,160
Allāh 'azwa jal says, I'll translate all of it first, Allāh is the One Who--

674
00:33:36,160 --> 00:33:39,055
Allāh in fact, He extracted you
from the bellies of your mothers

675
00:33:39,079 --> 00:33:40,220
while you knew nothing.

676
00:33:40,230 --> 00:33:41,210
It also translates,

677
00:33:41,640 --> 00:33:42,860
and you still know nothing.

678
00:33:43,540 --> 00:33:45,046
لَا تَعْلَمُونَ شَيْـًۭٔا

679
00:33:45,056 --> 00:33:48,600
could be ḥālīyah or i'tiradhiyah, and if it is ḥālīyah 'as you knew nothing',

680
00:33:48,650 --> 00:33:50,240
and by the way, you still know nothing.

681
00:33:50,260 --> 00:33:51,283
Okay?

682
00:33:51,308 --> 00:33:53,400
وَجَعَلَ لَكُمُ ٱلسَّمْعَ وَٱلْأَبْصَـٰرَ وَٱلْأَفْـِٔدَةَ

683
00:33:53,450 --> 00:33:54,360
and He placed for you

684
00:33:54,370 --> 00:33:59,280
He put for you in place the ability to see--to hear, to see and hearts.

685
00:33:59,305 --> 00:34:01,270
لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ
So you may become grateful

686
00:34:02,040 --> 00:34:05,070
أَلَمْ يَرَوْا۟ إِلَى ٱلطَّيْرِ مُسَخَّرَٰتٍۢ فِى جَوِّ ٱلسَّمَآءِ

687
00:34:05,095 --> 00:34:10,050
Haven't they looked to birds that are hung in the belly of the sky, in the middle of the sky.

688
00:34:10,739 --> 00:34:15,439
مَا يُمْسِكُهُنَّ إِلَّا ٱللَّهُ
Nobody's holding them in place except Allāh

689
00:34:15,539 --> 00:34:17,810
إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَـَٔايَـٰتٍۢ لِّقَوْمٍۢ يُؤْمِنُونَ

690
00:34:17,835 --> 00:34:19,400
In all of that, there certainly are

691
00:34:19,400 --> 00:34:21,679
miraculous signs for those who believe

692
00:34:21,679 --> 00:34:24,110
وَٱللَّهُ جَعَلَ لَكُم مِّنۢ بُيُوتِكُمْ سَكَنًۭا

693
00:34:24,270 --> 00:34:26,720
And Allāh put--made for you in your homes,

694
00:34:26,744 --> 00:34:30,860
a place in which you can find
stillness, comfort, calmness.

695
00:34:31,139 --> 00:34:33,563
وَجَعَلَ لَكُم مِّن جُلُودِ ٱلْأَنْعَـٰمِ بُيُوتًۭا

696
00:34:33,623 --> 00:34:38,393
and He also put in place for you, from the skins of animals, temporary homes you can make.

697
00:34:38,433 --> 00:34:41,273
تَسْتَخِفُّونَهَا
You find them light to carry on your backs.

698
00:34:41,313 --> 00:34:42,360
Tents basically

699
00:34:42,840 --> 00:34:44,389
made from the skins of animals.

700
00:34:44,400 --> 00:34:46,514
يَوْمَ ظَعْنِكُمْ وَيَوْمَ إِقَامَتِكُمْ

701
00:34:46,554 --> 00:34:49,304
The day you're going to go take off, the day your going stay

702
00:34:49,354 --> 00:34:53,384
وَمِنْ أَصْوَافِهَا وَأَوْبَارِهَا وَأَشْعَارِهَآ أَثَـٰثًۭا وَمَتَـٰعًا إِلَىٰ حِينٍۢ

703
00:34:53,460 --> 00:34:57,200
and you take from their wool and their hairs and their skins.

704
00:34:57,210 --> 00:34:59,940
You take them to make all kinds of goodness for yourselves

705
00:35:00,010 --> 00:35:02,060
and to enjoy them for a while.

706
00:35:02,160 --> 00:35:04,733
وَٱللَّهُ جَعَلَ لَكُم
مِّمَّا خَلَقَ ظِلَـٰلًۭا

707
00:35:04,757 --> 00:35:08,870
And Allāh put in place for you from
the things He created shadows, shade.

708
00:35:09,540 --> 00:35:10,580
The comfort of shade.

709
00:35:11,428 --> 00:35:13,588
وَجَعَلَ لَكُم مِّنَ ٱلْجِبَالِ أَكْنَـٰنًۭا

710
00:35:13,618 --> 00:35:15,878
And He put in place for you from the mountains--

711
00:35:15,948 --> 00:35:20,708
within the mountains He made caves for you to find refuge in as you travel.

712
00:35:20,740 --> 00:35:22,480
وَجَعَلَ لَكُمْ سَرَٰبِيلَ

713
00:35:22,560 --> 00:35:25,713
and He put in place for you the kinds of garments or clothing or gear

714
00:35:25,793 --> 00:35:28,443
تَقِيكُمُ ٱلْحَرَّ
that protects you from intense heat.

715
00:35:28,619 --> 00:35:30,553
وَسَرَٰبِيلَ
And other garments

716
00:35:30,673 --> 00:35:33,620
تَقِيكُم بَأْسَكُمْ
that protects you from war, meaning armor.

717
00:35:34,040 --> 00:35:37,832
كَذَٰلِكَ يُتِمُّ نِعْمَتَهُۥ عَلَيْكُمْ
That is how He completes His favor upon you

718
00:35:37,852 --> 00:35:38,810
لَعَلَّكُمْ تُسْلِمُونَ

719
00:35:38,810 --> 00:35:40,622
so you may be in submission.

720
00:35:40,742 --> 00:35:44,020
Now it seems kind of all over the place.

721
00:35:44,240 --> 00:35:46,550
It started with what? What do you recall?

722
00:35:46,560 --> 00:35:49,860
You came out of the bellies of your mothers.

723
00:35:50,340 --> 00:35:52,280
Let's take a step back and understand first and

724
00:35:52,280 --> 00:35:54,740
foremost that in that first of these Ayāt, Allāh 'azwa jal

725
00:35:54,740 --> 00:35:56,500
said that He put in place for you hearing,

726
00:35:56,500 --> 00:36:00,190
seeing and heart so you can become grateful.

727
00:36:00,340 --> 00:36:05,933
In other words, all of what is to follow is Allāh's way of getting us to become more what?

728
00:36:06,043 --> 00:36:08,893
Grateful from what we see and what we hear from Allāh.

729
00:36:08,913 --> 00:36:12,597
What we hear from Allāh
should effect how we see things

730
00:36:12,621 --> 00:36:15,620
and that should infect--effect our hearts.

731
00:36:15,630 --> 00:36:20,370
So there's a progressive relationship between hearing, seeing and the hearts.

732
00:36:20,370 --> 00:36:24,450
I'll repeat that, when you hear something, it changes the way you see things.

733
00:36:24,460 --> 00:36:28,064
Now that you see it differently, it effects your heart.

734
00:36:28,320 --> 00:36:30,570
So every time you see it, there's an impact on your heart.

735
00:36:30,590 --> 00:36:35,377
That's the kind of the A-B-C.
ٱلسَّمْعَ وَٱلْأَبْصَـٰرَ وَٱلْأَفْـِٔدَةَ ۙ

736
00:36:35,402 --> 00:36:38,740
That's highlighted here and how does it effect your heart? It makes you what?

737
00:36:39,230 --> 00:36:40,870
Grateful
لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ

738
00:36:40,850 --> 00:36:43,340
You with me so far? Okay, now let's begin.

739
00:36:44,030 --> 00:36:47,820
Allāh took you out of the bellies of your mothers. You were surrounded by comfort.

740
00:36:47,820 --> 00:36:50,130
Allah enveloped you in the belly of your mother.

741
00:36:50,180 --> 00:36:53,350
And the time came where you could no longer be surrounded by

742
00:36:53,350 --> 00:36:57,040
that perfect life that Allāh had enveloped you and wrapped you in.

743
00:36:57,110 --> 00:37:00,760
He had covered you in the bellies of your mothers and He took you out.

744
00:37:00,890 --> 00:37:03,160
Now that He's taking you out. Observe!

745
00:37:03,430 --> 00:37:06,840
Do you remember how you were in the belly of your mother? How He kept you there?

746
00:37:06,850 --> 00:37:09,960
You should think about how a bird is kept in the belly of the sky.

747
00:37:11,530 --> 00:37:13,100
Look at that sky hanging

748
00:37:13,125 --> 00:37:17,220
مُسَخَّرَٰتٍۢ فِى جَوِّ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَا يُمْسِكُهُنَّ إِلَّا ٱللَّهُ ۗ

749
00:37:17,260 --> 00:37:19,070
Nobody's holding them in place except Allāh.

750
00:37:19,080 --> 00:37:23,460
Just like nobody was holding you inside the belly of your mother except Allāh.

751
00:37:23,560 --> 00:37:26,250
Next time you see a bird, you remember what you were inside your mom.

752
00:37:27,330 --> 00:37:31,320
That bird is at the mercy of Allāh like you were at the mercy of Allāh.

753
00:37:31,330 --> 00:37:34,740
That bird, its world is the sky. Your world was the belly of your mother.

754
00:37:35,930 --> 00:37:39,460
Now, and that shold--looking at that bird should now enhance your faith.

755
00:37:39,830 --> 00:37:44,540
And by the way, even though you came out of the covering of your mother,

756
00:37:44,930 --> 00:37:46,460
Allāh gave you a new covering.

757
00:37:47,240 --> 00:37:49,995
وَٱللَّهُ جَعَلَ لَكُم مِّنۢ بُيُوتِكُمْ سَكَنًۭا

758
00:37:50,130 --> 00:37:52,950
He now covered you in the comfort of your homes.

759
00:37:53,830 --> 00:37:55,960
Just like your home used to be mom

760
00:37:56,330 --> 00:37:59,170
now your home is your your new mom in a sense,

761
00:37:59,180 --> 00:38:01,150
and you had sukūn inside your mom.

762
00:38:01,620 --> 00:38:05,540
There was no problem, no issues. And now your home has sakana in it.

763
00:38:05,920 --> 00:38:07,410
And even when you travel,

764
00:38:07,420 --> 00:38:13,030
you take the animal skin and make homes and cover yourselves by Allāh's mercy

765
00:38:13,060 --> 00:38:15,550
the way you did once you were in the bellies of your moms.

766
00:38:16,520 --> 00:38:18,950
And Allāh made it easy for you to be covered yet again,

767
00:38:20,220 --> 00:38:25,390
even when your staying or your moving along from its wool and its hair and its skin.

768
00:38:25,400 --> 00:38:30,180
And then He says: And I also by they way, even when you're not physically covered

769
00:38:30,220 --> 00:38:31,650
I cover you with shadows.

770
00:38:32,620 --> 00:38:36,080
وَٱللَّهُ جَعَلَ لَكُم مِّمَّا خَلَقَ ظِلَـٰلًۭا

771
00:38:36,420 --> 00:38:37,340
With shadows.

772
00:38:37,920 --> 00:38:42,350
And even when you are in the rough, rigid terrain of a mountain and a storm comes,

773
00:38:42,360 --> 00:38:45,440
I allow you to go into the belly of a mountain inside caves.

774
00:38:45,540 --> 00:38:46,900
وَمِنَ ٱلْجِبَالِ أَكْنَـٰنًۭا

775
00:38:48,020 --> 00:38:50,540
And even when there's no shadow and there's no

776
00:38:50,540 --> 00:38:52,920
cave and there's no other thing covering you,

777
00:38:52,930 --> 00:38:56,820
I gave you the cover of clothing that protects you from the intense heat.

778
00:38:56,820 --> 00:38:58,340
That's another covering I gave you.

779
00:38:59,720 --> 00:39:01,340
And even when you go to war,

780
00:39:01,340 --> 00:39:03,230
I taught you how to make a covering that will protect you

781
00:39:03,230 --> 00:39:07,130
from that kind of environment. Constantly protecting you,

782
00:39:07,140 --> 00:39:10,530
covering you, protecting you from the heat, protecting you with shade,

783
00:39:10,540 --> 00:39:12,490
protecting you, giving you sukūn in the home.

784
00:39:12,500 --> 00:39:17,860
Ya Allāh we never left that care of Allāh that was inside the bellies of our mothers

785
00:39:17,860 --> 00:39:19,840
now you appreciate when Allāh says you don't know anything.

786
00:39:21,620 --> 00:39:24,830
You and I think we were so helpless when we were inside our moms.

787
00:39:26,320 --> 00:39:28,030
Allāh reminds us actually,

788
00:39:28,420 --> 00:39:30,340
you're still inside your clothes.

789
00:39:30,820 --> 00:39:32,420
You're still inside a shade.

790
00:39:32,750 --> 00:39:34,330
You're still inside a home.

791
00:39:35,720 --> 00:39:39,250
You know you should remember that the bird is still inside the sky.

792
00:39:40,320 --> 00:39:44,360
And remember, you're still inside some level of 'رحمة' of Allāh.

793
00:39:44,370 --> 00:39:45,990
There's an Ayāh that's not here

794
00:39:46,060 --> 00:39:50,500
that unravels, unwraps pun intended all of this.

795
00:39:51,120 --> 00:39:54,950
Judgment Day, Allāh says
وَتَرَكْتُم مَّا خَوَّلْنَـٰكُمْ

796
00:39:56,220 --> 00:40:00,170
You have left behind all the wrappings We wrapped you in.

797
00:40:01,420 --> 00:40:03,150
All the covers We had placed on you.

798
00:40:03,620 --> 00:40:04,500
All of them are gone.

799
00:40:04,810 --> 00:40:05,750
Subḥānallāh.

800
00:40:06,720 --> 00:40:09,770
Allāh 'azwa jal keeping us secured in covering

801
00:40:10,070 --> 00:40:11,840
is the theme of this passage.

802
00:40:12,690 --> 00:40:15,190
The most obvious of which was the belly of the mother.

803
00:40:15,620 --> 00:40:17,550
But the rest of it wasn't as obvious.

804
00:40:17,560 --> 00:40:22,150
So He built it progressively, one by one by one by one by one. Subḥānallāh.

805
00:40:22,160 --> 00:40:26,320
Okay? So that's that's why Sūrat al-Nahl-yeah.

806
00:40:27,720 --> 00:40:29,450
Yeah, that's pretty sweet.

